    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0ad3973ef47ae188bbf5c5dcba23b0a0acfbc4a4502f4d7a7d5ef83d554077bd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proposed Virasoro extension encounters separable obstructions at successive representations: the original modular object has exponential cusp growth; cusp multiplication restores square-integrability but mixes spins; the Poisson-Mellin functional weakens decay enough to threaten convergence and leaves spin-dependent signs; and selecting a nonzero Fourier mode restores sporadic Maass data. The guessed c<7 scalar rule and the fixed-spin equation each remove only one part of this obstruction map.",
