    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1a2e5ed98f621ade167dedae807be4d49baf2904f6dd7ad71dd6c5cef9a3a2d9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After Eisenstein subtraction makes the reduced partition function square-integrable, averaging over the modular real part removes the Maass cusp sector while preserving Eisenstein constant modes. Identifying the surviving overlap with the constrained Epstein scalar series supplies analytic continuation and a functional equation; contour shifting then separates zeta-controlled residues from an explicit Mobius-hypergeometric kernel acting on scalar dimensions.",
