    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3bf9cfd640312ef6dece103933ffa319bdf977d99765957663f01c079411ee7c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Poisson resummation gives endpoint decay that makes the Mellin action entire and forces its value on a power t^s to contain zeta(s), so powers indexed by nontrivial zeros are annihilated. In the Virasoro application, however, the same integration changes exponential decay in dimension into exponential decay in its square root, which can lose to Cardy growth and is separate from the remaining spin-dependent sign obstruction.",
