    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_52d486f71945c15c1cbc953e2477bdf079d2b64b68c9c80d104f5c0591cb3bb7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Gaussian action provides a general special-function representation of the crossing terms, while odd central charge permits exact arithmetic resummation into finite or elementary kernels. Applying k^(3/2) times the k-derivative exposes an inversion-antisymmetric Bessel formulation that exists and converges for every c, showing that the odd-c closed forms are computational conveniences rather than the source of the crossing identity's validity.",
